2026-09-29 20:31 Design: parent binds (today's listen code, split out of start), removes the servers from its loop, runs discovery (router->list_models) + the capability probe to completion (->get, bounded by probe_timeout) BEFORE forking so workers inherit results; then drops pooled Net::Async::HTTP connections (loop->remove/add closes the pool) so no worker shares a keep-alive socket with another; forks N via plain fork + loop->post_fork (NOT loop->fork: it undefs ONE_TRUE_LOOP and engines/tracing lazily build their client on IO::Async::Loop->new); plain-perl waitpid supervisor with TERM/INT forwarding and restart backoff 1..30s for workers dying <5s after start. Workers _exit. RequestLog JSONL -> single syswrite under flock on O_APPEND.

